WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.435
A tick is one of the most

00:00:02.435 --> 00:00:04.804
 dangerous things on the planet.

00:00:04.804 --> 00:00:07.474
Even though it may not look like it.

00:00:07.474 --> 00:00:09.943
A single bite could affect you

00:00:09.943 --> 00:00:12.245
 for the rest of your life. 

00:00:12.245 --> 00:00:15.882
But how can this happen exactly? 

00:00:15.882 --> 00:00:17.117
On today's challenge, 

00:00:17.117 --> 00:00:18.385
we're going to show you

00:00:18.385 --> 00:00:19.886
what happens when you get

00:00:19.886 --> 00:00:21.588
 bitten by a tick.

00:00:31.431 --> 00:00:34.601
Ticks are not insects. 

00:00:34.601 --> 00:00:36.703
They're parasitic arachnids

00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:38.438
that can be as small as

00:00:38.438 --> 00:00:40.273
 a poppyseed.

00:00:40.273 --> 00:00:41.674
They are capable of

00:00:41.674 --> 00:00:43.443
carrying more diseases

00:00:43.443 --> 00:00:45.979
than any other arthropod.

00:00:45.979 --> 00:00:49.816
But not all ticks are disease carriers.

00:00:49.816 --> 00:00:51.184
The most common

00:00:51.184 --> 00:00:53.319
 disease-transmitting species is

00:00:53.319 --> 00:00:55.288
the black-legged tick,

00:00:55.288 --> 00:00:57.323
 also known as the deer tick.

00:00:57.323 --> 00:00:58.391
What if

00:00:58.391 --> 00:01:01.294
a disease-ridden deer tick bit you?

00:01:01.294 --> 00:01:04.030
How quickly would you feel the effects,

00:01:04.030 --> 00:01:05.498
if at all?

00:01:05.498 --> 00:01:08.101
You're hiking through a meadow of

00:01:08.101 --> 00:01:10.537
 tall grass on a warm spring day.

00:01:10.537 --> 00:01:12.038
Little do you know that 

00:01:12.038 --> 00:01:14.374
it's prime tick season, 

00:01:14.374 --> 00:01:16.943
and you'll be bringing home a stowaway. 

00:01:18.945 --> 00:01:22.215
Ticks don't always latch on right away.

00:01:22.215 --> 00:01:23.650
They sometimes spend 

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:25.318
an hour or two searching

00:01:25.318 --> 00:01:27.554
for the perfect place to feast, 

00:01:27.554 --> 00:01:30.090
often where there is thin skin

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:31.524
near a blood vessel.

00:01:31.524 --> 00:01:33.359
When a tick finally finds 

00:01:33.359 --> 00:01:36.463
the perfect place to extract your blood,

00:01:36.463 --> 00:01:39.399
 it burrows its head into your skin. 

00:01:39.399 --> 00:01:41.568
It unleashes a feeding tube

00:01:41.568 --> 00:01:43.736
 and secretes blood-thinning, 

00:01:43.736 --> 00:01:45.605
skin-numbing saliva.

00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:47.507
Not only did it bite you,

00:01:47.507 --> 00:01:49.542
 but you didn't even feel it.

00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:51.511
Yuck.

00:01:53.513 --> 00:01:56.149
The tick has likely been feeding on 

00:01:56.149 --> 00:01:58.618
a moist area on your body, 

00:01:58.618 --> 00:02:00.720
 like your groin or armpits.

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:01.888
And by now,

00:02:01.888 --> 00:02:03.923
 the tick is much larger

00:02:03.923 --> 00:02:05.125
than a poppyseed, 

00:02:05.125 --> 00:02:07.160
 having gorged on your blood 

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:09.529
for over 24 hours.

00:02:09.529 --> 00:02:11.464
There are many diseases 

00:02:11.464 --> 00:02:13.099
transmitted by ticks, 

00:02:13.099 --> 00:02:14.868
 like the Powassan virus and

00:02:14.868 --> 00:02:17.103
 the Rocky Mountain spotted fever.

00:02:17.103 --> 00:02:18.738
But the most well-known

00:02:18.738 --> 00:02:20.106
tick-borne ailment

00:02:20.106 --> 00:02:22.542
 is Lyme disease.

00:02:22.542 --> 00:02:25.211
A 2014 study found that

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:27.747
only one to three percent of people

00:02:27.747 --> 00:02:30.216
bitten by a tick carrying Lyme disease 

00:02:30.216 --> 00:02:31.751
will become infected.

00:02:31.751 --> 00:02:34.320
But the Centers for Disease Control 

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:35.722
and Prevention says

00:02:35.722 --> 00:02:37.190
the number of reported

00:02:37.190 --> 00:02:38.591
 cases of Lyme disease

00:02:38.591 --> 00:02:39.959
 in the United States

00:02:39.959 --> 00:02:43.096
 has tripled since the late 1990s.

00:02:43.096 --> 00:02:45.865
Luckily, disease transmission

00:02:45.865 --> 00:02:48.368
 is not instantaneous.

00:02:48.368 --> 00:02:50.904
The CDC says that if the tick is

00:02:50.904 --> 00:02:53.439
removed within 24 hours, 

00:02:53.439 --> 00:02:54.474
your chances of 

00:02:54.474 --> 00:02:56.609
getting Lyme disease are low.

00:02:56.609 --> 00:02:58.244
Unfortunately,

00:02:58.244 --> 00:03:01.147
 you continue to go about your day,

00:03:01.147 --> 00:03:02.415
 not realizing that

00:03:02.415 --> 00:03:04.551
there's a blood-sucking parasite

00:03:04.551 --> 00:03:06.286
 attached to your body.

00:03:08.288 --> 00:03:11.691
You've finally noticed the tick

00:03:11.691 --> 00:03:13.993
as it has become engorged

00:03:13.993 --> 00:03:15.695
 and grown to three times 

00:03:15.695 --> 00:03:17.230
its original size. 

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:19.232
That's nasty.

00:03:19.232 --> 00:03:22.535
Now it's time to remove it.

00:03:22.535 --> 00:03:25.672
Get some tweezers and grasp the tick

00:03:25.672 --> 00:03:28.074
 close to your skin's surface. 

00:03:28.074 --> 00:03:31.110
Pull straight up and away from the skin,

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:32.879
 applying steady pressure.

00:03:32.879 --> 00:03:36.516
Do not bend or twist the tick. 

00:03:36.516 --> 00:03:39.485
Next, check the bite site to see if

00:03:39.485 --> 00:03:42.055
any of the tick’s head remains

00:03:42.055 --> 00:03:43.590
and carefully remove it.

00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:46.526
Clean the bite with soap and water. 

00:03:46.526 --> 00:03:48.628
Then submerge the tick 

00:03:48.628 --> 00:03:50.063
in rubbing alcohol

00:03:50.063 --> 00:03:51.831
 to make sure it's dead.

00:03:51.831 --> 00:03:55.001
You'd notice a solid red oval that

00:03:55.001 --> 00:03:57.770
looks like a bulls-eye at the bite site. 

00:03:57.770 --> 00:04:00.206
Meh, it's probably nothing.

00:04:00.206 --> 00:04:03.276
It'll go away in a couple of days, right? 

00:04:05.278 --> 00:04:08.081
The tick debacle is behind you. 

00:04:08.081 --> 00:04:10.016
But much to your dismay,

00:04:10.016 --> 00:04:12.719
it left a sinister parting gift.

00:04:12.719 --> 00:04:14.954
The red bulls-eye remains

00:04:14.954 --> 00:04:16.322
 at the bite site.

00:04:16.322 --> 00:04:19.559
You've developed a full-body rash.

00:04:19.559 --> 00:04:22.028
And over the past four weeks, 

00:04:22.028 --> 00:04:24.063
 you've had persistent headaches,

00:04:24.063 --> 00:04:25.465
neck stiffness, 

00:04:25.465 --> 00:04:27.233
and aches everywhere.

00:04:27.233 --> 00:04:30.303
Plus, you're nauseous.

00:04:30.303 --> 00:04:32.305
As the month has progressed, 

00:04:32.305 --> 00:04:35.608
you're experiencing a fever and chills.

00:04:35.608 --> 00:04:36.676
You notice that

00:04:36.676 --> 00:04:38.911
 your lymph nodes are swollen.

00:04:38.911 --> 00:04:41.214
You assume it's just a bug

00:04:41.214 --> 00:04:42.715
 and not the blood-sucking, 

00:04:42.715 --> 00:04:44.217
disease-carrying kind.

00:04:44.217 --> 00:04:46.085
So you take some painkillers 

00:04:46.085 --> 00:04:47.220
and ride it out.

00:04:49.222 --> 00:04:50.490
After months,

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:52.225
 your symptoms have gotten

00:04:52.225 --> 00:04:53.626
 even worse.

00:04:53.626 --> 00:04:56.429
 On top of feeling sick all the time, 

00:04:56.429 --> 00:04:58.164
you've also had a hard time

00:04:58.164 --> 00:05:01.200
 concentrating and remembering things.

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:04.404
You've finally decided to see a doctor.

00:05:04.404 --> 00:05:06.272
You've been diagnosed with 

00:05:06.272 --> 00:05:07.940
Lyme disease.

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:10.910
If you spotted this tick six months ago

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:13.112
 and went to the doctor right away,

00:05:13.112 --> 00:05:14.747
this disease would've been

00:05:14.747 --> 00:05:16.249
 easier to treat.

00:05:16.249 --> 00:05:17.850
You may not have even gotten it

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:19.218
 in the first place.

00:05:19.218 --> 00:05:22.322
You’ll need antibiotics right away.

00:05:22.322 --> 00:05:23.823
Luckily there is hope 

00:05:23.823 --> 00:05:25.892
you'll get back to normal.

00:05:25.892 --> 00:05:29.028
But it could be a long road to recovery.

00:05:29.028 --> 00:05:32.098
Even after antibiotics,

00:05:32.098 --> 00:05:33.800
 people who have Lyme disease 

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:35.501
can experience symptoms

00:05:35.501 --> 00:05:37.837
for up to six months.

00:05:37.837 --> 00:05:40.606
But if you seek medical attention,

00:05:40.606 --> 00:05:43.376
 you will eventually recover.

00:05:43.376 --> 00:05:45.611
"I got better!"

00:05:45.611 --> 00:05:47.580
Hopefully, you can avoid 

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:49.282
something like this happening.

00:05:49.282 --> 00:05:50.316
 After all, 

00:05:50.316 --> 00:05:52.752
the key to preventing Lyme disease

00:05:52.752 --> 00:05:55.488
is making sure a tick never latches 

00:05:55.488 --> 00:05:57.256
onto you in the first place.

00:05:57.256 --> 00:05:59.459
When exploring the outdoors,

00:05:59.459 --> 00:06:00.927
wear long pants 

00:06:00.927 --> 00:06:03.730
with socks pulled up over your ankles.

00:06:03.730 --> 00:06:05.231
After you get home, 

00:06:05.231 --> 00:06:06.666
check for ticks,

00:06:06.666 --> 00:06:08.368
especially on your head,

00:06:08.368 --> 00:06:09.202
legs, 

00:06:09.202 --> 00:06:10.370
and ankles.

00:06:10.370 --> 00:06:12.438
 And don't forget to check your pets.

00:06:12.438 --> 00:06:15.341
 A tick bite can affect them as well.

00:06:15.341 --> 00:06:17.410
Although getting a tick bite

00:06:17.410 --> 00:06:18.578
can come with

00:06:18.578 --> 00:06:20.813
some serious consequences,

00:06:20.813 --> 00:06:23.549
you did manage to survive.

00:06:23.549 --> 00:06:26.119
But what about another challenge

00:06:26.119 --> 00:06:29.222
 with a far lower survival rate,

00:06:29.222 --> 00:06:32.859
like being allergic to everything?

00:06:32.859 --> 00:06:33.926
Well,

00:06:33.926 --> 00:06:36.529
we'll see what that challenge brings

00:06:36.529 --> 00:06:38.531
on the next episode of

